In the proof that a quadrilateral whose diagonals bisect each other is a parallelogram, $\triangle ABE \cong \triangle CDE$ is shown by SAS.
Which pair of equal angles is the "A" in that SAS?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{arrows.meta,decorations.markings,calc,angles,quotes}
\tikzset{sa/.style={postaction={decorate,decoration={markings,mark=at position 0.5 with {\arrow{Stealth}}}}},da/.style={postaction={decorate,decoration={markings,mark=at position 0.4 with {\arrow{Stealth}},mark=at position 0.56 with {\arrow{Stealth}}}}},tk/.style={postaction={decorate,decoration={markings,mark=at position 0.5 with {\draw (0pt,-4pt)--(0pt,4pt);}}}},tk2/.style={postaction={decorate,decoration={markings,mark=at position 0.5 with {\draw (-2pt,-4pt)--(-2pt,4pt);\draw (2pt,-4pt)--(2pt,4pt);}}}}}
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (4.6,0);
\coordinate (C) at (6.1,2.5);
\coordinate (D) at (1.5,2.5);
\draw (A)--(B);
\draw (B)--(C);
\draw (C)--(D);
\draw (D)--(A);
\coordinate (E) at (3.05,1.25);
\draw[tk] (A)--(E);
\draw[tk] (E)--(C);
\draw[tk2] (B)--(E);
\draw[tk2] (E)--(D);
\node[above left] at (3.2,1.4) {$E$};
\node[below left] at (A) {$A$};
\node[below right] at (B) {$B$};
\node[above right] at (C) {$C$};
\node[above left] at (D) {$D$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

